WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:05.670
When faced with complex questions on a patient's condition or the need for how-to

2
00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:10.440
answers from evidence-based literature, there's a solution nurses and allied health

3
00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:15.691
professionals can turn to and trust. Welcome to ClinicalKey for Nursing.

4
00:00:16.831 --> 00:00:21.270
This short video will demonstrate how nurses and allied health professionals can

5
00:00:21.331 --> 00:00:25.951
take advantage of the wealth of clinical knowledge and dynamic features available

6
00:00:26.010 --> 00:00:30.510
on ClinicalKey for Nursing to empower them in their role and aid their daily

7
00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:35.940
activities. In the minutes ahead, we will highlight ways to access the product's

8
00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:41.580
broad range of content, outline the steps to earn CE credits, and showcase best

9
00:00:41.610 --> 00:00:44.911
practices for creating and using a personal account.

10
00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:49.770
Through ClinicalKey for Nursing, nurses and allied health professionals have a

11
00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:54.810
single location to find market-leading content across multiple specialties.

12
00:00:55.620 --> 00:01:00.840
The product includes over 60 top journals, 85 full textbooks,

13
00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:06.961
and hundreds of practice guidelines, patient education handouts, procedural

14
00:01:06.990 --> 00:01:12.030
videos, and more. These offerings cover more than 20 specialties,

15
00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:17.910
including critical care, emergency medicine, internal medicine, and

16
00:01:17.970 --> 00:01:23.520
pediatrics. Some examples include "Clinical Companion to Medical Surgical

17
00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:28.980
Nursing," "Saunders Nursing Drug Handbook," "American Journal of Infection

18
00:01:29.071 --> 00:01:34.650
Control," "Heart &amp; Lung," "Journal of Pediatric Health Care," and

19
00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:36.840
"Burn's Pediatric Primary Care."

20
00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:42.540
To locate content, users can turn to the browse and search functions.

21
00:01:43.290 --> 00:01:48.150
By clicking a category under the browse menu, users are automatically directed to

22
00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:53.970
its full collection. On the homepage, the content type to browse is selected here.

23
00:01:54.450 --> 00:01:59.610
For example, books. The browse books page displays a list of available

24
00:01:59.641 --> 00:02:03.090
publications, which can be filtered by title or alphabetically.

25
00:02:04.170 --> 00:02:09.060
Inside each book, a digital table of contents provides quick access to chapters.

26
00:02:10.051 --> 00:02:14.310
On all other pages of ClinicalKey for Nursing, the browse option is at the top of

27
00:02:14.370 --> 00:02:19.620
the screen here. From the browse drop-down menu, several additional content types

28
00:02:19.650 --> 00:02:22.020
can be chosen. For example, journals.

29
00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:27.480
On the browse journals page, navigate to a journal title the same way as for books.

30
00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:32.790
Once a title has been chosen, the journal's homepage lists volumes and issues.

31
00:02:33.601 --> 00:02:36.180
Note the Search This Journal feature below the title.

32
00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:41.460
This enables users to parse content and discover information on a specific topic.

33
00:02:43.230 --> 00:02:47.700
For point-of-care materials, return to the browse menu and select Clinical

34
00:02:47.851 --> 00:02:52.710
Overviews. These condition summaries offer bullet-pointed, peer-reviewed

35
00:02:52.770 --> 00:02:57.990
recommendations toward differential diagnoses, causes and risk factors, treatment

36
00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:00.630
options and drug therapies, and much more.

37
00:03:01.770 --> 00:03:05.820
Content can also be found on ClinicalKey for Nursing through a standard search.

38
00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:11.040
Notice that the filter to the left of the search bar can easily help save time by

39
00:03:11.101 --> 00:03:13.830
limiting results to a certain content type.

40
00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:18.990
For some topics, a disease overview preview box will display on the right.

41
00:03:19.710 --> 00:03:24.570
Similar to clinical overviews, disease overviews provide clear recommendations on a

42
00:03:24.630 --> 00:03:28.921
patient's condition. They also include a section on nursing management, which

43
00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:33.360
offers more information on patient goals, intervention, and teaching.

44
00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:38.970
Continuing education credits can be obtained via ClinicalKey for Nursing when

45
00:03:39.031 --> 00:03:43.830
reviewing clinical updates. To do so, nurses will need to perform the following

46
00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:46.890
steps. Visit a relevant clinical update.

47
00:03:47.550 --> 00:03:51.840
This can easily be done by, once again, using the browse menu and choosing the

48
00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:57.480
clinical updates category. After selecting a clinical update, click the Go to Test

49
00:03:57.541 --> 00:04:01.470
link on the right side to be redirected to Elsevier's learning management system.

50
00:04:02.281 --> 00:04:06.300
Those who have not previously earned CE credits through ClinicalKey for Nursing

51
00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:10.470
should first select the self-registration link to create a user profile.

52
00:04:11.550 --> 00:04:15.300
Once logged in, the list of e-learning lessons appears under the Current

53
00:04:15.390 --> 00:04:20.550
Assignments menu. Find the clinical update of choice by scrolling the lesson list

54
00:04:20.671 --> 00:04:25.350
or performing a quick search, inputting the title and choosing the filter Contains.

55
00:04:26.130 --> 00:04:28.920
The lesson now appears with the option Take the Test.

56
00:04:29.701 --> 00:04:34.080
Completing the set of multiple-choice questions allows nurses to earn a CE

57
00:04:34.170 --> 00:04:34.860
certificate.

58
00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:40.830
Creating a personal account opens up new user features on ClinicalKey for Nursing,

59
00:04:41.190 --> 00:04:44.970
including the ability to save content and export images.

60
00:04:45.690 --> 00:04:50.160
To set up a personal user profile, click Register in the upper right corner of the

61
00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:55.440
screen. Note that when completing the form, an organizational email address should

62
00:04:55.470 --> 00:05:00.390
be entered for the username. Once registered, users can now take advantage of

63
00:05:00.451 --> 00:05:04.710
valuable saving and exporting features when reviewing content in ClinicalKey for

64
00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:05.281
Nursing.

65
00:05:06.750 --> 00:05:11.220
Personalization features can be accessed by clicking the drop-down under the user's

66
00:05:11.281 --> 00:05:15.420
name, which now appears in the upper right corner instead of Register.

67
00:05:16.201 --> 00:05:20.070
To demonstrate these features, we'll use an image in a journal article as an

68
00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:25.201
example. When encountering an image or figure of interest, users can click on the

69
00:05:25.290 --> 00:05:30.960
star to save it. They also can select the screen icon to add it to a presentation,

70
00:05:31.050 --> 00:05:32.820
which can be exported to PowerPoint.

71
00:05:33.570 --> 00:05:37.260
Now that this image has been saved, it will appear in Saved Content.

72
00:05:37.980 --> 00:05:41.100
From here, users can add tags to organize their listings.

73
00:05:41.850 --> 00:05:44.701
They also can add multiple images to a presentation.

74
00:05:46.140 --> 00:05:50.760
Another important benefit of registering is that it enables users to activate their

75
00:05:50.820 --> 00:05:56.160
remote capabilities so they can access ClinicalKey for Nursing anywhere, anytime.

76
00:05:56.970 --> 00:06:01.560
For details about setting up remote access or when faced with a product question or

77
00:06:01.650 --> 00:06:05.190
issue, look to Elsevier's Support Center for assistance.

78
00:06:05.701 --> 00:06:07.740
A link can be found at the bottom of any page.

79
00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:12.900
The Support Center is where nurses and allied health professionals will find FAQs

80
00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:17.520
for a variety of product questions and channels for contacting our customer service

81
00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:19.740
via phone, chat, and email.

82
00:06:21.451 --> 00:06:24.750
The depth and breadth of ClinicalKey for Nursing doesn't end here.

83
00:06:25.290 --> 00:06:28.680
To experience all the value the product has to offer, visit

84
00:06:28.890 --> 00:06:33.000
www.clinicalkey.com/nursing today.
